{"page_content": "S\n\ntep 2: normalise the NOEC for the 3 BLM species towards site- specific/region-specific average and rwc conditions\n\nA\n\nccording to the Zn EU RAR, both average (= 50% of pH, hardness and DOC for the 3 BLM species) and reasonable worst-case conditions RWC (= 10% of pH, hardness and DOC for fish & invertebrates; 10% of hardness and DOC, 90% of pH for algae) were used to normalize the NOEC values for the 3 different BLM organisms. This will result in different NOECx values for the 3 BLM species normalised towards the conditions in the river, as shown in Table 13\n\nT\n\nable 13: Overview of the normalised NOEC (\u00b5g/l) for the BLM species", "metadata": {"doc_id": "cf35ef07-a48c-436d-95e0-f4fddb1d99b1", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "information_requirements_r7_13_2_en.pdf"}}